{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{\\coprod_{i \\in I} T_i \\to T\\}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-by-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1914912c1515d2a5da8af4fae74fb9b39b660ba7731ac0cc418c679e550c0eec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:320dbe065b26065df037cb2a3b312815096088c1d29120bb41b435f6d07fa84f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a family\nof morphisms. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is a V covering,\n<STRUCT_0003> there is a V covering which refines <MATH_0004>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0005> is a V covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a93675ccf81cbfaf74bc9c81eff14bb81e186a32f807d17a8d138cef118a2745", "unit_id": "tag:0ETI:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-refine-by-ph}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbf24626c675b3478451ae2f8f7ce86f4b67efeeec1dcfdb772accb966d86363", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: compare with the proof of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:912538f05aa3ff64c4821db2b28a8ed657f8a86d24f72dfcb3b308a7aedc2ebc", "unit_id": "tag:0ETI:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29ad49eac91d31053f37bed8fc43a14e1f43d6d8adc878d46039be5cdd2f38df", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis a V covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a V covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have a V covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is a V covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is a V covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is a V covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8dce0da747587ca225ffd988df9d2faa0ef142312cbc5522b0530d35bf0c62f", "unit_id": "tag:0ETJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U' \\subset T'$", "MATH_0002": "$U'$", "MATH_0003": "$U' = U'_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup U'$", "MATH_0004": "$U'_j \\to T$", "MATH_0005": "$U_j \\subset T$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_{jl} \\to U_j\\}_{l = 1, \\ldots, n_j}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U_j \\to U_j\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_{jl} \\times_{U_j} U'_j \\to U'_j\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{U'_j \\to U'\\}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{U_{jl} \\times_{U_j} U'_j \\to U'\\}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{U_{jl} \\times_{U_j} U'_j \\to U'\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U' \\to U'\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\subset T$", "MATH_0014": "$\\{U_k \\to U\\}_{k = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$U_k \\to T_{i_k}$", "MATH_0017": "$T$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\{T_{i_kj} \\times_{T_{i_k}} U_k \\to U_k\\}_{j \\in J_{i_k}}\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$U_k$", "MATH_0020": "$\\{U_{ka} \\to U_k\\}_{a = 1, \\ldots, b_k}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\{U_{ka} \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\{T_{ij} \\times_T U \\to U\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-standard-V}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-standard-fpqc-standard-V}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-standard-V}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-composition-standard-V}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:290a3540f0f269fa4df408825bc640045cf5dac59055e0825c3fe9401c537f40", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a11603eae09d5a386e7cafce40df587715b09586474d803fcfeef8c29a0d160a", "source_text": "Assertion (1) is clear.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nProof of (3).\nLet <MATH_0001> be an affine open subscheme.\nSince <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact we can find a finite affine open\ncovering <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004> maps into an affine open <MATH_0005>.\nChoose a standard V covering <MATH_0006>\nrefining <MATH_0007>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe base change <MATH_0008>\nis a standard V covering. Note that <MATH_0009>\nis a standard V covering\n(for example by Lemma <REF_0002>).\nBy Lemma <REF_0003> \nthe family <MATH_0010>\nis a standard V covering. Since\n<MATH_0011> refines <MATH_0012>\nwe conclude.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nProof of (2).\nLet <MATH_0013> be affine open. First we pick a standard V covering\n<MATH_0014> refining\n<MATH_0015>.\nSay the refinement is given by morphisms <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>.\nThen\n<MATH_0018>\nis a V covering by part (3). As <MATH_0019> is affine,\nwe can find a standard V covering\n<MATH_0020> refining this family.\nThen we apply Lemma <REF_0004>\nto see that <MATH_0021> is a standard V covering which\nrefines <MATH_0022>. This finishes the proof.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b2aef16047f72483a2cd4f30a03cfb00cc66257610da258f3bf2df058707a97", "unit_id": "tag:0ETJ:proof"}
